I have analyzed the issue and applied a fix.

### Why the Gradient Hover Effect Wasn't Showing
1. **Flex Container vs. `background-clip: text`**: 
   The `<a>` element has class `flex` (which resolves to `display: flex` or `display: inline-flex` via `.button-secondary`). Standard browser rendering engines (like Chrome/Blink and Safari/WebKit) do not correctly clip a background gradient to text when the element is a **flex container** containing child elements (like the `<ArrowRight>` SVG). Instead, it tries to clip the background to the outer boundary of the flex items, or renders nothing at all.
2. **Undefined CSS Color Variable**:
   In `src/index.css`, `.button-secondary` had `color: var(--text);`, but there is no `--text` variable defined in your `:root`. I've corrected this to use `color: var(--foreground);`.

---

### The Fix Applied
To resolve the gradient hover rendering bug while retaining the flex layout and the SVG arrow alignment:
1. **Updated the HTML/JSX** in [About.tsx](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/jasmijn-schrofer/src/components/home/About.tsx) (line 50) and [Featured.tsx](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/jasmijn-schrofer/src/components/home/Featured.tsx) (line 68) to wrap the text nodes in a `<span>` element:
   ```html
   <span>Read full bio</span>
   ```
2. **Updated the CSS rules** in [index.css](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/jasmijn-schrofer/src/index.css):
   - Corrected the default color variable.
   - Applied the hover gradient, text clip, and transparent color directly to the `span` element rather than the parent flex container.
   ```css
   .button-secondary {
     @apply px-6 py-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2;
     color: var(--foreground);
     transition: all 0.5s ease-in-out;
   }

   .button-secondary:hover span {
     background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
     background-clip: text;
     -webkit-background-clip: text;
     color: transparent;
   }
   ```

